  "reasons": {
   "pie-lex-kjerh2wos": "Gk κεραός (oxytone; Beekes EDG s.v., < *kerh₂u̯-o-) is the adjective 'horned'; the substantive 'the horned one, deer' may retract the accent (Fortson §6.72, cf. the Hróth₂os override), and Beekes posits an ablauting *kerh₂-u-o-/*kr̥h₂-eu-o-: undecided",
   "pie-lex-gjhleystos": "no accented source; Celtic reflexes only (Wiktionary ǵʰley-), no Vedic or Greek",
   "pie-lex-werdhom": "every source prints it unaccented (de Vaan s.v. verbum, Kroonen p. 600, Derksen, NIL, Handbook vol. 3 ch. 8); no Vedic or Greek reflex",
   "pie-lex-h1eh2nos": "no accented source (de Vaan s.v. ānus, M&A *ānos, Matasović); Latin, Celtic, Armenian reflexes only",
   "pie-lex-h2eysos": "formation in doubt, not only the accent: de Vaan s.v. aeruscō has an s-stem neuter *h₂eis-os- (aeruscō < *aisos-ko-), Wiktionary's only reflex; Ved. eṣá- m. (EWAia I 270) would give h₂eysós only if the thematic masculine is kept",
   "pie-lex-srowmos": "no accented source (Kroonen, Beekes EDG *srou-mo-); Germanic reflex only; Gk ῥεῦμα, ῥόος are other formations",
   "pie-lex-gurnos": "no accented source (M&A *gu-r-nos); Baltic and Armenian reflexes only (Lith. gurnas AP 4 decides nothing by itself)",
   "pie-lex-wexdos": "no accented source (Kroonen *u̯ēd-o-, NIL); Germanic reflex only",
   "pie-lex-h1rudhyos": "no accented source for the -yo- formation (Balto-Slavic reflex only); Ved. rudhirá-, Gk ἐρυθρός are the -ró- formation (Fortson *h₁rudʰ-ró-)",
   "pie-lex-teh2yeti": "only a synonym list on Wiktionary's tinéh₁ti page prints téh₂yeti; LIV² p. 616 has a *teh₂-i̯e- present but its accent is not legible here; no Vedic or Greek ye-present: too weak for a checked spec",
   "pie-lex-h2emseti": "no accented source; Anatolian only (LIV² p. 269 ?perfect, Hitt. ḫāši; Kloekhorst), a ḫi-verb rather than a thematic present"
  },
  "reasons_note": "Searched 2026-10-24 for the 11 lexemes of the stored non-pilot Tier 3 corpus (Fortson, Ringe, Beekes, M&A, LIV², EDG, EWAia, de Vaan, Kroonen, Derksen, Matasović, NIL, Wiktionary's other pages); none has a sourced accent that decides it, so none got an override. LIV²'s OCR copy here loses accent marks."
 },
