  "ids": {
   "pie-lex-skweyteh2yeti": "headword skʷéyteh₂yéti carries two accents (root and suffix); a denominative *-eh₂-yé- would take the suffix accent alone (Ved. -āyáti)",
   "pie-lex-h1eh1ughtos": "headword h₁éh₁ugʰtós carries two accents",
   "pie-lex-h1eh1ughyos": "headword h₁éh₁ugʰyós carries two accents",
   "pie-lex-pipreh1ti": "headword pípréh₁ti carries two accents; the shape rule copies both into the strong stem",
   "pie-lex-plenh1onti": "headword plénh₁ónti is a 3pl with two accents; the shape rule parses it as a 3sg stem plénh₁ón- (athematic-verbs.md)",
   "pie-lex-megjyoxs": "the Wiktionary table's loc. sg. méǵh₂yés carries two accents (an acrostatic stem has the root accent only)"
